# Testing and quality

- Pure utils (formatting, Jalali dates, text normalization, status→actions maps, query-key factories) have unit
  tests. These are shared by many services, so a bug there multiplies.
- Shared pattern hooks (approval, soft delete, categories, reasons) have tests against mock `api/` including every
  E-path.
- Test names include SRS codes where they verify a path.
- E2E: the CI `e2e` target must correspond to a real project. Until a Playwright project exists, do not add tests
  that pretend to be e2e; record the gap in `docs/09-known-issues.md`.
- No skipped or `.only` tests committed. No lowering lint rules to make a change pass.
- Use `docs/templates/testing-checklist.md` before merging a feature.
